# History: rcan-assurance. RCAN's canonical JSON section says that names sort in "Unicode
# code-point order" and, in the same section, that the scheme "matches RFC 8785", which sorts by
# UTF-16 code units. No published test vector told the two apart, and the two SDKs disagreed
# past the published vectors.
#
# Written as duramen, the section binds two edges to one operation. The checker compares their
# conformance packs and reports the input where they disagree (T026), with no oracle and no
# implementation: {"｡":1,"😀":2}, where code-point order and UTF-16 order differ. (Both edges
# refuse strings with lone surrogates, which cannot be written as the raw UTF-8 that RCAN's
# rules ask for, so they agree there.)
duramen 0.1

spec rcan-canonical 3.2

op canonical
  input value any

edge json/sorted-codepoint via canonical value
edge json/rfc8785 via canonical value
